# The Acid palette

<!--
  Generated by acidify from docs/palette.md.tera. Do not edit; edit the template,
  or the palette in crates/acid-palette/src/lib.rs, and re-run `make docs`.
-->

Acid is a very dark colourscheme in the spirit of gruvbox: warm text, earthy
accents, and no colour that fights the code for attention. It comes in two
flavours.

| Flavour | Background | Accents |
| --- | --- | --- |
{% for identifier, flavor in flavors -%}
| **{{ flavor.name }}** (`{{ identifier }}`) | `{{ flavor.colors.base }}` | {% if identifier == "acetic" %}Vibrant{% else %}Muted{% endif %} |
{% endfor %}
Every colour below carries its contrast ratio against its own flavour's `base`,
measured per WCAG 2.1. Accents and text tones are all at or above 4.5:1, which
is the AA threshold for body text.
{% for identifier, flavor in flavors %}
